# CODEOWNERS
#
# GitHub reads this file and automatically requests review from the listed
# owners when a PR touches a matching path. Combined with branch protection's
# "require review from Code Owners", it becomes mandatory rather than polite.
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS MORE THAN IT LOOKS
#
# Not all files carry the same risk. A change to a README and a change to the
# deploy workflow are both "one file changed" in a PR summary, but one of them
# can exfiltrate your cloud credentials. CODEOWNERS is how you make the risky
# paths pull in the people who understand them, automatically, without relying
# on anyone noticing.
#
# SYNTAX
#   Same pattern rules as .gitignore.
#   LAST matching rule wins -- ordering is significant, most general first.
#   Owners are @user or @org/team.
#
# NOTE: in this practice repo every owner is the same person, which makes the
# reviews self-approvals. In the boot camp, replace these with real teammates
# and the mechanism starts doing actual work.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default -- everything not matched more specifically below
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                           @mangohero8

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Application code
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
/app/                       @mangohero8
/tests/                     @mangohero8

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HIGH RISK -- pipeline and infrastructure
#
# Anything under .github/workflows/ is code GitHub executes on its runners
# with access to repository secrets and, in the deploy workflow, the ability
# to mint cloud credentials. A malicious or careless change here is far more
# dangerous than a bug in the application.
#
# In a real org these paths belong to a platform or security team, and that
# separation is the point: the people who can change the pipeline should not
# be the same set as everyone who can change a handler.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/workflows/         @mangohero8
/.github/dependabot.yml     @mangohero8
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @mangohero8
/Dockerfile                 @mangohero8
/.dockerignore              @mangohero8
/scripts/                   @mangohero8

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependency manifests -- where supply chain risk enters
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
/requirements.txt           @mangohero8
/requirements-dev.txt       @mangohero8

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cross-platform behaviour -- easy to change, breaks everyone on the other OS
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.gitattributes             @mangohero8
